WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.339
Data types should reflect meaning rather than only
the way a value

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:10.165
looks A generated identifier can use an identity
column Exact

00:00:10.191 --> 00:00:16.138
monetary values are better represented with an exact
numeric type Whole-number quantities

00:00:16.165 --> 00:00:22.099
use integer types General descriptive text can use
text Birth

00:00:22.112 --> 00:00:25.967
dates use date while real-world moments such as
appointment times often use

00:00:25.994 --> 00:00:31.765
timestamp with time zone Boolean is appropriate for
genuinely true-or-false

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:37.443
states Throughout this course we also use common
PostgreSQL style

00:00:37.456 --> 00:00:42.061
conventions uppercase SQL keywords lower snake case
for table and column names

00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:47.916
and identity columns rather than MySQL-style
AUTO_INCREMENT Do

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:52.182
not choose a type only because a sample value fits
Choose the

00:00:52.209 --> 00:00:55.853
type that represents the meaning and the rules the
database should enforce
